---
import SectionHeading from "./SectionHeading.astro";
import { asset } from "../lib/paths";
---

<section id="qualitative" class="section container">
  <SectionHeading
    number="06"
    label="Qualitative evidence & limitations"
    title="The difficult cases are part of the story."
    description="Curated annotation examples, not a model leaderboard. Dense scenes, occlusion and language-grounding errors remain open challenges."
  />
  <div class="qualitative-grid">
    <figure>
      <img
        src={asset("assets/counting/0001-640.webp")}
        width="640"
        height="360"
        loading="lazy"
        alt="Dense fish school above a reef, IOCfish5K 0001"
      />
      <figcaption>
        <span class="micro-label">Dense scenes · sample 0001</span>
        <h3>270 points. Uneven visibility.</h3>
        <p>
          134 clear, 130 ambiguous and 6 highly camouflaged instances. A single
          total conceals how differently targets can appear.
        </p>
        <span class="source-note">Final annotations · visibility summary</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <img
        src={asset("assets/counting/5044-640.webp")}
        width="640"
        height="360"
        loading="lazy"
        alt="Fish partially occluded by underwater structure, sample 5044"
      />
      <figcaption>
        <span class="micro-label">Occlusion · sample 5044</span>
        <h3>Presence is not always obvious.</h3>
        <p>
          20 point annotations include 6 clear, 11 ambiguous and 3 highly
          camouflaged instances, reflecting difficult boundaries between visible
          evidence and interpretation.
        </p>
        <span class="source-note">Final annotations · visibility summary</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <img
        src={asset("assets/counting/0000-density.webp")}
        width="1280"
        height="720"
        loading="lazy"
        alt="Precomputed density heatmap for sample 0000"
      />
      <figcaption>
        <span class="micro-label">Density evidence · sample 0000</span>
        <h3>A hotspot is not a causal claim.</h3>
        <p>
          Four stored hotspots connect local density to scene evidence.
          Ecological explanations remain hypotheses requiring expert review.
        </p>
        <span class="source-note">Final annotations · density hotspots</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <details class="limitation-detail">
    <summary>When language and structured evidence disagree</summary>
    <div class="error-comparison">
      <div>
        <span class="micro-label">Released QA · sample 0001, pair 3</span>
        <blockquote>
          “The densest grid area is 'top-right' (top-right corner), with 70
          fish”
        </blockquote>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="micro-label">Structured annotation</span>
        <p>
          <strong>Top-center: 87. Top-right: 70.</strong> The released answer
          overlooks the actual maximum. The explorer preserves the structured
          values; the source QA file is not modified.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="source-note">
      A concrete annotation-quality failure, not a measured model prediction.
      Numeric consistency checks and semantic review remain necessary.
    </p>
  </details>
  <div class="limitations">
    <h3>What Nereus does not establish</h3>
    <p>
      Coverage is uneven across taxa, geography, depth and imaging devices.
      Automated localization and multimodal annotation can introduce noise.
      Image-level degradation labels do not measure local water quality or
      hidden biological states. Results do not show universal gains across every
      metric, and the manuscript reports no error bars.
    </p>
    <span class="source-note">Limitations · pp. 9, 15–16; checklist p. 24</span>
  </div>
</section>
